CS225 HW6
Create a class called Monster. The Monster class has a strength member variable
that is not public (select private or protected). The Monster class should have a
default constructor that randomly assigns a strength value between 1 and 30. The
Monster class has a member function: speak(which prints “Boo”) and getStrength
(which returns the strength). Create a static data member that keeps track of the
number of monsters created.
Derive 3 classes from Monster: Zombie, Werewolf, and Vampire. All 3 child
classes inherit everything from the parent, but they all have their own version of the
speak function. Create default constructors for each class that prints: “it’s a
______”(Zombie, Vampire, or Werewolf)
In main, create an array of 5 Monster pointers. Ask the users to select which
monster they would like to face each time through the loop and dynamically allocate
memory for that type of monster.
After all the monsters have been created, loop through the array of pointers and call
the speak member function for each object. Print the total strength of all monsters
added together. You must release all the memory you dynamically allocated
before the program ends.
